  "result": "Perfect! I've successfully created the customer statements module. Here's what was implemented:\n\n## Changes\n\n**src/statements.js** \u2013 New customer statement module:\n\n1. **`statement(customerId, invoices, asOf)`** function that:\n   - Normalizes and validates the customer exists (CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND error)\n   - Filters invoices to only include:\n     - The specified customer\n     - Status 'issued' or 'partially_paid' (excludes draft and paid)\n     - issueDate on or before the asOf date (inclusive)\n   - Returns `ok({ customerId, invoices, totalDue })` where:\n     - `invoices` is sorted by issueDate ascending\n     - Each invoice includes: `{ number, issueDate, dueDate, total, due }`\n     - `due` is calculated from `balanceDue()` (reflects any partial payments)\n     - `totalDue` is the sum of all due amounts\n\n**test/statements.test.js** \u2013 25 comprehensive tests covering:\n- Empty invoice lists\n- Customer filtering and normalization\n- Unknown customer error handling\n- Status filtering (excludes draft and paid, includes issued/partially_paid)\n- Date filtering (asOf date boundary conditions)\n- Sorting by issueDate\n- Invoice data completeness (number, issueDate, dueDate, total, due)\n- Partial payment reflection in due calculations\n- Multiple customer handling\n- Edge cases (missing fields, empty lists)\n\n**Test Results**: All 199 tests pass (174 previous + 25 new)",
